      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm I think this hasn\u0027t changed apart from renaming ?\n\nI meant factoring out most of the code from this method and the one below to a common method.\n\nThe previous naming actually looked better as it\u0027s getting a config, not actually using it.\n\nThis logic is really hard to follow because it sets variables to some defaults and then overwrites the values; but in the end it calculates:\n - newDelayUntilNextTaskWithoutBackoffMs\n - newExpectUnicastResponse\n - newTimeBetweenBurstsInMs\n\nI think it would be clearer if you can refactor it to use methods like:\n\n```\nlong getDelayUntilNextTask(isFirstBurst, isFirstQueryInBurst, isLastQueryInBurst) {\n    if (isFirstQueryInBurst \u0026\u0026 queryMode \u003d\u003d AGGRESSIVE) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n    if (isLastQueryInBurst) {\n        return timeBetweenBurstsInMs;\n    }\n    return queryMode \u003d\u003d AGGRESSIVE\n        ? TIME_BETWEEN_RETRANSMISSION_QUERIES_IN_BURST_MS\n        : TIME_BETWEEN_QUERIES_IN_BURST_MS;\n}\n\nboolean getNextExpectUnicastResponse(isFirstQueryInBurst) {\n    if (alwaysAskForUnicastResponse) {\n        return true;\n    }\n    return queryMode \u003d\u003d AGGRESSIVE \u0026\u0026 isFirstQueryInBurst;\n}\n\nlong getNextTimeBetweenBurstsMs(boolean isLastQueryInBurst) {\n    if (!isLastQueryInBurst) {\n        return timeBetweenBurstsInMs;\n    }\n    final long maxTimeBetweenBursts \u003d queryMode \u003d\u003d AGGRESSIVE\n            ? MAX_TIME_BETWEEN_BURSTS_MS : TIME_BETWEEN_BURSTS_MS);\n    return Math.min(maxTimeBetweenBursts, timeBetweenBurstsInMs * 2);\n}\n```\n\nThen you should be able to use mostly common code for `isFirstBurst`, and `burstCounter`",
